KVM: s390: Fix gmap_helper_zap_one_page() again

jira KERNEL-1864
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-6.12.0-264.7.1.el10_3
commit-author Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
commit 2f393c228cc519ddf19b8c6c05bf15723241aa96
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-6.12.0-264.7.1.el10_3/2f393c22.failed

A few checks were missing in gmap_helper_zap_one_page(), which can lead
to memory corruption in the guest under specific circumstances.

Add the missing checks.

Fixes: 5deafa27d9ae ("KVM: s390: Fix to clear PTE when discarding a swapped page")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Reported-by: Marc Hartmayer <mhartmay@linux.ibm.com>
	Tested-by: Marc Hartmayer <mhartmay@linux.ibm.com>
	Acked-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2f393c228cc519ddf19b8c6c05bf15723241aa96)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	arch/s390/mm/gmap_helpers.c
diff --cc arch/s390/mm/gmap_helpers.c
index c382005577bd,d41b19925a5a..000000000000
--- a/arch/s390/mm/gmap_helpers.c
+++ b/arch/s390/mm/gmap_helpers.c
@@@ -63,9 -66,13 +64,18 @@@ void gmap_helper_zap_one_page(struct mm
  	if (pte_swap(*ptep)) {
  		preempt_disable();
  		pgste = pgste_get_lock(ptep);
+ 		pgstev = pgste_val(pgste);
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		ptep_zap_swap_entry(mm, pte_to_swp_entry(*ptep));
 +		pte_clear(mm, vmaddr, ptep);
++=======
+ 		if ((pgstev & _PGSTE_GPS_USAGE_MASK) == _PGSTE_GPS_USAGE_UNUSED ||
+ 		    (pgstev & _PGSTE_GPS_ZERO)) {
+ 			ptep_zap_softleaf_entry(mm, softleaf_from_pte(*ptep));
+ 			pte_clear(mm, vmaddr, ptep);
+ 		}
++>>>>>>> 2f393c228cc5 (KVM: s390: Fix gmap_helper_zap_one_page() again)
  
  		pgste_set_unlock(ptep, pgste);
  		preempt_enable();
* Unmerged path arch/s390/mm/gmap_helpers.c
